{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"df60b5debff62306566f1b91b86b4279862a253991048597493c25ad9b617801","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review model-ladder escalation","key_entities":["MODEL_LADDER","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","claude-haiku-4-5","claude-sonnet-4-6","claude-opus-4-8","models_at_or_above","escalation_rungs","pass1_with_ladder","prerequisites.run_focused_finder","largest_window_tokens","max_input_tokens"],"problem_keywords":["context-limit escalation","ladder rung","no-op escalation","wasted spend","misleading diagnosis","model window capacity"],"propositions":["Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 4.8 both declare a 1,000,000 token window in MODEL_LADDER, making escalation from sonnet to opus a guaranteed no-op that still incurs opus pricing and fails with identical context-limit error.","Context-limit escalation loops must skip rungs whose declared windows are not strictly greater than the last kept rung, to prevent paid calls that cannot succeed.","New function escalation_rungs() filters models_at_or_above() output to remove equal-window rungs, while models_at_or_above() and MODEL_LADDER contents remain unchanged to preserve provider stickiness and size budget.","Both context-limit retry loops (pass1_with_ladder and prerequisites.run_focused_finder) must consume escalation_rungs() instead of models_at_or_above() to avoid the no-op escalation defect."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787320292725029001,"uuid":"4acb515e-7666-4c00-9918-a49a0c0daba0"}